{"n": 422, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "422.webp", "text": "24-146\n\nExplanations tor Independent Electronic Transmission\nContro} (AEGS):\n\nThere4s a comprehensive test of the entire AEGS each\ntime the engine ts started,\n\nTurn on ignition.\n\nThe yellow defect indicator lamp in the instrument\npanel will flash twice and must stay on while starting\nand go out at an engine speed above 450 rpm.\n\nTest Position Detect Indicator\n\nRepair wire to wiring diagram.\nRepair wire to wiring diagram .\n\nBreak in ground wire 5/19.\nCheck voltage between wires 5/19 and 24 with the\nignition on,\n\nNominal value: approx. 5 V.\nAEGS control unit defective.\n\nDetect indicator does not flash and remains on after starting.\n\nReplace control unit 24 61 000.\n\nPower supply to AEGS control unit insufficient. Repair wire to wiring diagram.\nCheck voltage between wires 5/19 and 35 with the\nignition on.\n\nNominal valde: > 10 V.\n\nWires to solenoid 1 (Y1), 2 (¥2), reverse gear (Y4)\nor converter lockup clutch (¥3) have a break or are\ngrounded out.\n\nSee test plan for checking.\n\nNo TD signal from DME control unit.\n\nNo ti signal from DME control unit.\n\nDetect mdicator flashes, but remaims on after starting.\n\nRepair wires to wiring diagram.\n\nCheck plug connection (X) and power supply lead to\nAEGS control unit.\n\nPower supply between wires 5/19 and 35 insufficient Repair wires to wiring diagram,\n(drops below 10 V).\n\nTD signal stops suddenly.\n\nBreak in positive wires to solenoids.\n\nDefect mdicator comes on while driving,\n\nRepair wires to wiring diagram.\n\nTroubleshooting — also refer to Service Information 24 02 85 (422).", "words": [["24-146", 0.4574, 0.0332, 0.5339, 0.057], ["Explanations", 0.0542, 0.0716, 0.1155, 0.0842], ["tor", 0.1185, 0.0716, 0.1317, 0.0829], ["Independent", 0.1358, 0.0723, 0.1945, 0.0849], ["Electronic", 0.1986, 0.0716, 0.2467, 0.0829], ["Transmission", 0.2508, 0.0716, 0.3131, 0.0822], ["Contro}", 0.0537, 0.0875, 0.0902, 0.0988], ["(A